{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויאכלו", :translit "vayokhlu", :gloss "and they ate"} {:he "ויאמרו אליו", :translit "vayomru elav", :gloss "and they said to him"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The narrative shift from 'they ate' directly to 'they said to him' signals that they did not converse during the meal itself."}], :frame {:text "The Talmud warns that one must not converse during a meal, lest the windpipe precede the esophagus and cause choking — i.e., food may enter the trachea while talking (Taanit 5b). Ba'al HaTurim reads the seamless transition from 'and they ate' to 'and they said to him' as reflecting this principle: the angels ate in silence and only spoke after the meal concluded.", :sources ["Taanit 5b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The narrative shift from 'they ate' directly to 'they said to him' signals that they did not converse during the meal itself.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:06:28.948585189Z", :model "glm-5.2"}